version: 0.2.1
abstract: Xi yi xin fa [New methods of Western medicine] is a late-Qing Chinese work
  on surgery and bandaging, credited to John Glasgow Kerr for oral translation and
  Lin Xiangdong for written rendering. The catalogue for Bodleian Sinica 1826 supplies
  [Canton] and [1872]. Based on 25 images, the dataset provides TXT, JSON and TEI
  XML for 44 designated physical faces, with uncertainties and source mappings for
  research on medical translation, bandaging history and image-text relationships.
  The provisional AI transcription includes selected source-image corrections; full
  human double collation and expert review have not been performed.
